From 83ad675b9e5c85aeb5a6caebb1ba363a98eb5253 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:22:31 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: CPU thermal
 trips mirroring stock

kaanapali.dtsi gives the CPU and CPU-LLC thermal zones only hot (120 C) and critical (125 C) trips, so the
CPUs would run unthrottled up to the critical shutdown. Under full load they reach 105 C in about 4 s.

Use the stock 11.A.38 values per zone:
- CPU zones: 105 C (hysteresis 5 C; stock thermal HAL), then 112 C (4 C) and 114 C (6 C) (stock kernel
  emergency stages)
- CPU-LLC zones: 112 C and 114 C only (stock has no HAL trip there)

Stock pauses CPUs at 112/114 C. Mainline has no pause cooling device, so the 105 C stage throttles cpufreq
step by step, the 112 C stage clamps it to at least half the cooling states, and the 114 C stage to the
lowest frequency. The cooling states are those of this unit's OPP tables: cpu0-5 0..27, cpu6-7 0..28.
Passive polling is 10 ms, as for the kaanapali GPU zones.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
